  "finalText": "The 12-second password manager scene is built in the Main comp across the three beats, on a cream background with a flat navy, coral, teal and amber palette.\n\n- **Beat 1, problem (0–3.6 s):** six sticky notes with passwords pop in with Back Out and jitter anxiously until about 3.6 s.\n- **Beat 2, gather (3.3–4.7 s):** the vault shield pops in at 3.3 s. The notes are pulled into its center on Expo In arcs, spinning and shrinking as they go, and the shield gives a small bump as the last one lands.\n- **Beat 3, resolve (4.2–12 s):** a soft amber glow breathes behind the shield. A teal check mark draws on (7.0–7.5 s), then \"One key. Every login.\" rises in below it and holds to the end.\n\nThe critique scored it 75/100. I fixed the shield bump's abruptness. The remaining flags are deliberate: the notes passing behind the shield is the suction itself, and the even note cadence is a sequential pull.\n\nTwo changes from the storyboard timing: the notes finish their suction at about 4.7 s rather than 7.5 s, so beat 2 is shorter than planned, and the headline lands at 7.4 s instead of 7.5 s. I can stretch the suction or add a hold if you want the gather to breathe more.\n\nNext options: a word-by-word headline reveal, or a slightly brighter glow pulse."
